diff --git a/docs/labs/linux.md b/docs/labs/linux.md
index 63ee43f..9946c91 100644
--- a/docs/labs/linux.md
+++ b/docs/labs/linux.md
@@ -111,6 +111,12 @@ LLDP is started on Ubuntu virtual machines if the **netlab_lldp_enable** group v
 
 To enable LLDP on Ubuntu virtual machines, set the **netlab_lldp_enable** node parameter or **defaults.devices.linux.group_vars.netlab_lldp_enable** variable to **True**.
 
+### LLDP on KNE Linux hosts
+
+Linux hosts running under the **kne** provider use the **lldp** attribute instead; LLDP is **off** by default. Set **lldp** to *True* on a node (or on a group through **node_data**, or **defaults.devices.linux.lldp**) to run LLDP on that host. A link-level or per-interface **lldp** attribute (for example `- h1: { lldp: true }` in a link definition) selects the individual interface and overrides the node setting for that interface; a node with **lldp: true** whose interfaces are all set to *False* runs no LLDP.
+
+The attribute is accepted only on devices that declare the *lldp* feature (**linux** with the **kne** provider). Using it on any other device, or putting a link-level **lldp** on a link whose other end is such a device, stops the topology with *Device X does not support lldp*; set it on the Linux end of the link only.
+
 (linux-dhcp-relay)=
 ## DHCP Relaying on Linux
 
